# Adobe Fonts Web Project ID (the short ID from https://use.typekit.net/XXXXXXX.css)
# <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://use.typekit.net/qal8vjr.css">
PUBLIC_ADOBE_FONTS_PROJECT=qal8vjr

# ActiveCampaign lead-capture proxy — HTTP API /ac/subscribe URL.
# This is the ONLY client-visible AC value (an endpoint URL, not a secret). It
# is the `ApiEndpoint` CloudFormation Output, e.g.
# https://{apiId}.execute-api.{region}.amazonaws.com/ac/subscribe
PUBLIC_AC_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://tbrubqn47k.execute-api.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/ac/subscribe

# NOTE: all non-public ActiveCampaign config lives on the Lambda, never here:
#   - AC_API_KEY  -> AWS Secrets Manager (read server-side at runtime)
#   - AC_API_URL, AC_LIST_ID, AC_TAGS, AC_FIELD_* -> Lambda env (CloudFormation)
# Do NOT add an AC_API_KEY or any AC_* server var to this file or to any
# PUBLIC_-prefixed variable — doing so would leak it into the client bundle.
